511.3 Coordinate‑Free Algebra Relational Tensioner (CART)

This document maps all CART components, operators, axioms, inference rules,
and relational modes across the full 511.3 CART corpus. It shows how each
file relates to the others and how the five-part substrate interlocks.


------------------------------------------------------------
0. CART SUBSTRATE (MASTER REFERENCE)
------------------------------------------------------------
CART = (C, K, D, C/K, H)

C   = Carrier (raw relational field)
K   = Kernel (tension-resolution operator)
D   = Defect (residual relational tension)
C/K = Quotient (identity formation)
H   = Hierarchy (relational entanglement depth)

Every other CART document references these five components.


------------------------------------------------------------
1. CROSS‑REFERENCE: CART → AXIOM SYSTEM
------------------------------------------------------------
CART AXIOM SYSTEM defines the formal laws governing each component.

Carrier axioms:
    C1–C4  → define raw relational field

Kernel axioms:
    K1–K5  → define resolution, idempotence, contractivity

Defect axioms:
    D1–D5  → define residual tension, zero-defect identity

Quotient axioms:
    Q1–Q6  → define identity formation, admissibility

Hierarchy axioms:
    H1–H6  → define ultrametric depth, tier structure

Cross‑link:
    Every axiom corresponds directly to one of the five CART components.


------------------------------------------------------------
2. CROSS‑REFERENCE: CART → INFERENCE CALCULUS
------------------------------------------------------------
The inference calculus provides reasoning rules for each component.

Resolution rules:
    R‑Intro, R‑Idempotent, R‑Resolved-Judgment
    → correspond to Kernel axioms K1–K5

Defect rules:
    D‑Def, D‑Zero-Defect, D‑Monotonicity
    → correspond to Defect axioms D1–D5

Identity rules:
    Q‑Equiv-Def, Q‑Class-Formation, Q‑Canonical-Rep
    → correspond to Quotient axioms Q1–Q6

Hierarchy rules:
    H‑Ultrametric, H‑Tier-Assignment, H‑Tier-Monotonicity
    → correspond to Hierarchy axioms H1–H6

Composite inference patterns:
    Resolve → Defect → Identity → Hierarchy
    → matches the canonical CART operator pipeline.


------------------------------------------------------------
3. CROSS‑REFERENCE: CART → OPERATOR ALGEBRA
------------------------------------------------------------
The operator algebra defines how the five operators compose.

Identity operator:
    Id laws → relate to C (Carrier) and K (Kernel)

Kernel operator:
    K laws → match K axioms and resolution rules

Defect operator:
    D laws → match D axioms and defect rules

Quotient operator:
    Q laws → match Q axioms and identity rules

Hierarchy operator:
    H laws → match H axioms and hierarchy rules

Operator composition:
    KD, QK, HQ, HK, HD
    → correspond to inference calculus composite patterns

Canonical pipeline:
    x → K → D → Q → H
    → corresponds to relational-mode transitions R0→R4.


------------------------------------------------------------
4. CROSS‑REFERENCE: CART → RELATIONAL-MODE DECOMPOSITION
------------------------------------------------------------
Relational modes correspond directly to CART components:

R0 Raw Mode      → Carrier (C)
R1 Resolution    → Kernel (K)
R2 Defect        → Defect (D)
R3 Identity      → Quotient (C/K)
R4 Hierarchy     → Hierarchy (H)

Mode transitions:
    R0 → R1 → R2 → R3 → R4
    → correspond to operator pipeline K, D, Q, H

Mode questions:
    R0: What exists?
    R1: What is its canonical form?
    R2: How far from resolved?
    R3: Who/what is it?
    R4: How deep is it?

Cross‑link:
    Each relational mode is the “phenomenological view” of one CART operator.


------------------------------------------------------------
5. CROSS‑REFERENCE: CART → PLANTUML DIAGRAM
------------------------------------------------------------
PlantUML diagram nodes correspond exactly to CART components:

Carrier      → C
Kernel       → K
Defect       → D
Quotient     → C/K
Hierarchy    → H
Tier enum    → H axioms (tier structure)
Ultrametric  → H axioms (distance structure)

Diagram arrows:
    Carrier → Kernel → Defect → Quotient → Hierarchy
    → matches operator algebra and inference calculus pipeline.


